ince our teammate passed, they may not have strong cards either.\n\nTherefore, **playing the 9-triplet + JJ pair** is the only move that beats the landlord and allows us to seize control, potentially allowing us or our teammate to play smaller cards safely later.\n\nReason:  \nWe must break the landlord’s momentum. Our teammate passed, indicating weakness. By playing the only winning combination available — ♥9 ♣9 ♦9 ♠J ♣J — we take control of the board, disrupt the landlord’s rhythm, and gain the lead for our side. Though we lose some strength, we retain decent follow-up plays. Not playing would cede advantage permanently.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥9", "♣9", "♦9", "♠J", "♣J"]}'}
